"post_office","la":47.600238,"lo":-122.334402,"d":1302},{"n":"Chase","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":47.621583,"lo":-122.338191,"d":1359,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-17:00; Sa-Su closed","w":"https://locator.chase.com/wa/seattle/350-westlake-ave-n","ph":"+1-206-447-3010"},{"n":"Victor Steinbrueck Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.61,"lo":-122.343889,"d":8,"ds":"Victor Steinbrueck Park is an urban park in Downtown Seattle, Washington, United States, located just northwest of Pike Place Market overlooking Elliott Bay. Named for the Seattle-based architect Victor Steinbrueck, it is positioned between Western Avenue and Alaskan Way at the foot of Virginia Street. The 0.8-acre (0.32 ha) park opened in 1971 and underwent major renovations from 2019 to 2025.","wpu":"Victor Steinbrueck Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Victor_Steinbrueck_Park%2C_Seattle.jpg/960px-Victor_Steinbrueck_Park%2C_Seattle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Emmett Watson's Oyster Bar","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.6101,"lo":-122.3427,"d":98,"ds":"Emmett Watson's Oyster Bar is a seafood restaurant in Seattle's Pike Place Market, in the U.S. state of Washington. Seattle journalist Emmett Watson and his friend Sam Bryant opened the city's first oyster bar on February 18, 1979. The restaurant is now operated by Bryant's son Thurman.","wpu":"Emmett Watson's Oyster Bar","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Pike_Place_Market_-_Emmett_Watson%27s_01.jpg/960px-Pike_Place_Market_-_Emmett_Watson%27s_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Virginia Inn","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.610861,"lo":-122.342639,"d":139,"ds":"Virginia Inn is a bar and restaurant in Seattle, Washington's Pike Place Market. Located in the Hotel Livingston, the Inn opened in 1903, four years before the Market. The establishment was a filming location for Sleepless in Seattle and Singles.","wpu":"Virginia Inn","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Seattle_%28November_2%2C_2022%29_-_34.jpg/960px-Seattle_%28November_2%2C_2022%29_-_34.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Overlook Walk","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.608611,"lo":-122.342778,"d":179,"ds":"Overlook Walk is a bridge over Alaskan Way in Seattle, in the U.S. state of Washington. Completed in 2024, the bridge serves as a pedestrian path to connect the Central Waterfront district and Pike Place Market. Construction on the project began in June 2022.","wpu":"Overlook Walk","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Seattle_-_Overlook_Walk_01.jpg/960px-Seattle_-_Overlook_Walk_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pike Place Fish Market","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.609425,"lo":-122.3417,"d":183,"ds":"Pike Place Fish Market is an open-air fish market at Pike Place Market in Seattle, Washington, United States, located at the corner of Pike Street and Pike Place. Founded in 1930, it is known for its tradition of fishmongers throwing the fish purchased by customers before wrapping it.","wpu":"Pike Place Fish Market","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Pike_Place_Fish_1.jpg/960px-Pike_Place_Fish_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Crystal Pool (Seattle)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.612222,"lo":-122.343056,"d":257,"ds":"Crystal Pool Natatorium was a saltwater indoor swimming pool in Seattle, Washington. It was eventually adapted and became the building of the Bethel Temple Pentecostal Church. It was designed by B. Marcus Priteca and built from 1915 to 1918.","wpu":"Crystal Pool (Seattle)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/Crystal_Pool_natatorium%2C_2035_2nd_Ave_at_Lenora_St%2C_Seattle_%28CURTIS_456%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Moore Theatre","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.611792,"lo":-122.341347,"d":281,"ds":"Moore Theatre is an 1,800-seat performing arts venue in Seattle, Washington, United States, located two blocks away from Pike Place Market at the corner of 2nd Avenue and Virginia Street. It opened in 1907 and is Seattle's oldest active theater, hosting a variety of theatrical productions, concerts and lectures.","wpu":"Moore Theatre","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/MooreSeattle.jpg/960px-MooreSeattle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Rachel (Gerber)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.608611,"lo":-122.340833,"d":283,"ds":"Rachel, also known as Market Foundation Piggy Bank, Rachael the Pig, Rachel the Pig or Rachel the Piggy Bank, is an outdoor bronze sculpture of a piggy bank, designed by Georgia Gerber and located at Pike Place Market in Seattle, Washington, in the United States. It was dedicated on August 17, 1986, the market's 79th birthday, and is maintained by the Pike Place Market Foundation.","wpu":"Rachel (Gerber)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/PikePlacePigWithPlaque.jpg/960px-PikePlacePigWithPlaque.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Helios (building)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":47.6108,"lo":-122.3398,"d":327,"ds":"Helios, also known as 2nd & Pine, is a residential skyscraper in downtown Seattle, Washington. The 40-story tower is 440 feet (130 m) tall with 398 luxury apartments. Plans for the project were first proposed in 2013 and construction began in late 2014.","wpu":"Helios (building)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Helios_%282nd_%26_Pine%29_from_Columbia_Center.jpg/960px-Helios_%282nd_%26_Pine%29_from_Columbia_Center.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Seattle ( see-AT-əl) is the most populous city in the U.S. state of Washington and the Pacific Northwest region of North America. It is the 18th-most populous city in the United States with a population of 784,777 in 2025, while the Seattle metropolitan area at over 4.15 million residents is the 15th-most populous metropolitan area in the nation. The city is the county seat of King County, the most populous county in Washington.","wpu":"Seattle","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Seattle_Center_as_night_falls.jpg/960px-Seattle_Center_as_night_falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}